TINarrativeEventTemplate.displayName.event_EEO_ExperimentalNotice=Notice to EEO Players
TINarrativeEventTemplate.event_EEO_ExperimentalNotice.summary=PLEASE MAKE SURE TO READ THIS! You might get blindsided by some things otherwise.<br><br>Welcome to Economic Equalization Overhaul's experimental branch. This introduction is intended for players who aren't aware of the recent update to the mod; if you've read the workshop description for the new version, posted in early March 2026, then you can stop reading.<br><br>For players who subscribed to this mod to play with EEO on pre-release versions of Terra Invicta, this mod no longer does that. EEO Experimental is now for testing new features, and EEO will only ever be kept updated to the latest release version of Terra Invicta.<br><br>The current experiment, and the reason for me making this pop-up message in the first place, is that the way investments are calculated has been fundamentally changed. All countries now produce the exact same amount of IP. Investments now use simulated IP, which are based on the exact same formulas the main branch uses. Basically, investments happen much less frequently, but still have the same large-scale effects. This was done to reduce late-game lag.<br><br>Some investment types will have varying IP costs across countries due to it being impossible to split it up across real investment points. This is particularly noticeable in armies and mission control. Their cost goes down as GDP goes up and vice versa. This is where simulated IPs come most into play. Other investment types, like funding and spoils, use simulated IP and will give varying amounts depending on the GDP of a country.<br><br>These changes should not meaningfully change the balance of the mod. If all goes right on my end, then EEO Experimental should play near-identically to the base mod. Countries should develop roughly the same, build armies roughly the same speed, and so on. They should also have the same relative IP drains from armies and navies.
TINarrativeEventTemplate.event_EEO_ExperimentalNotice.query=<skip/>
TINarrativeEventTemplate.event_EEO_ExperimentalNotice.option0=Continue
